00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:40.780
How far is it?

689
00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:41.700
Less than five.

690
00:29:42.000 --> 00:29:42.440
What?

691
00:29:42.760 --> 00:29:44.360
It's such a big difference.

692
00:29:44.600 --> 00:29:47.460
Why didn't anyone look that up at the writer's room?

693
00:29:47.460 --> 00:29:47.780
I don't know.

694
00:29:48.100 --> 00:29:51.000
But it's only like four hours and 45 minutes.

695
00:29:51.460 --> 00:29:52.680
Are you kidding me?

696
00:29:52.700 --> 00:29:53.760
I'm not kidding you.

697
00:29:53.960 --> 00:29:55.540
What roads were they taking?

698
00:29:55.540 --> 00:29:57.040
Are there new freeways?

699
00:29:57.320 --> 00:30:02.340
There were some, like, fan theories that it took them seven hours in that big truck.

700
00:30:02.960 --> 00:30:06.480
But that's not how we present it in this episode.

701
00:30:06.640 --> 00:30:09.560
We present it like, how are they ever going to see each other?

702
00:30:09.700 --> 00:30:14.580
Like, Holly says, even if you leave right after work, Michael, you won't even get here till after midnight.

703
00:30:14.880 --> 00:30:16.640
And then we'll just have one day together.

704
00:30:16.820 --> 00:30:18.180
And you'll have to go back.

705
00:30:18.220 --> 00:30:19.200
But it's not true.

706
00:30:19.360 --> 00:30:20.580
They really scared themselves.

707
00:30:21.060 --> 00:30:24.400
I mean, at four hours, they're in the middle of nowhere.

708
00:30:24.620 --> 00:30:25.800
That's how we sell it.

709
00:30:26.080 --> 00:30:26.560
Exactly.

710
00:30:26.840 --> 00:30:27.260
Oh, wow.

711
00:30:27.480 --> 00:30:28.020
I know.

712
00:30:28.220 --> 00:30:32.760
So, anyway, I just wanted to say that I also did check the train schedule.

713
00:30:32.960 --> 00:30:36.760
For a reason I can't explain, it takes over 12 hours on the train.

714
00:30:37.140 --> 00:30:39.380
Maybe our writers checked the train schedule.

715
00:30:39.600 --> 00:30:40.420
I don't know.

716
00:30:40.800 --> 00:30:42.560
A lot of stops, though, I guess.

717
00:30:42.740 --> 00:30:43.780
Oh, my gosh.

718
00:30:43.980 --> 00:30:44.180
Yeah.

719
00:30:44.740 --> 00:30:45.220
I know.

720
00:30:45.440 --> 00:30:46.580
Are you checking my work?

721
00:30:46.620 --> 00:30:47.540
You got your phone out.

722
00:30:47.660 --> 00:30:49.320
She is checking my work.

723
00:30:49.320 --> 00:30:50.100
I'm not checking.

724
00:30:50.100 --> 00:30:50.600
What do you think?

725
00:30:50.600 --> 00:30:52.980
I don't know how to Google Scranton to Nashua.

726
00:30:53.520 --> 00:30:54.980
No, I'm very curious.

727
00:30:55.000 --> 00:30:58.660
After all of my great information I've given you about rabies.

728
00:30:58.960 --> 00:31:00.460
Can I tell you something right now?

729
00:31:00.580 --> 00:31:00.880
What?

730
00:31:01.480 --> 00:31:02.520
I'm doing it, too.

731
00:31:02.700 --> 00:31:04.940
We're both Googling Scranton to Nashua.

732
00:31:05.620 --> 00:31:06.380
There it is.

733
00:31:06.480 --> 00:31:07.140
Five hours.

734
00:31:07.500 --> 00:31:09.020
It's 311 miles.

735
00:31:09.360 --> 00:31:09.800
Done.

736
00:31:09.980 --> 00:31:13.060
You know what's amazing is that a lot of people have written about this.

737
00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:13.940
I know.

738
00:31:14.040 --> 00:31:14.900
There's a whole Reddit thread.

739
00:31:15.020 --> 00:31:15.380
I know.

740
00:31:15.480 --> 00:31:16.680
I'm looking at the Reddit thread.

741
00:31:16.840 --> 00:31:17.120
See?

742
00:31:17.620 --> 00:31:18.060
Okay.

743
00:31:18.060 --> 00:31:21.140
Well, this shouldn't have broken them up.

744
00:31:21.660 --> 00:31:22.920
It really shouldn't have.

745
00:31:22.920 --> 00:31:24.720
They should have picked a further branch.

746
00:31:25.120 --> 00:31:25.360
Okay.

747
00:31:25.660 --> 00:31:26.640
Well, all right.

748
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:30.800
Speaking of all of these driving scenes, should we get into it a little bit?

749
00:31:31.260 --> 00:31:31.920
We'll come back.

750
00:31:32.160 --> 00:31:35.660
Stuff is happening back at the office with Dwight and Andy, but we'll get back to it.

751
00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:36.520
Should we do the driving?

752
00:31:36.640 --> 00:31:37.060
Let's do it.

753
00:31:37.120 --> 00:31:38.040
Let's get to the driving.

754
00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:38.560
Sam.

755
00:31:46.040 --> 00:31:47.680
All night long.

756
00:31:50.440 --> 00:31:57.850
If you're going for something all night long.

757
00:31:58.030 --> 00:31:58.290
Okay.

758
00:31:58.290 --> 00:32:00.070
Tom Cochran.

759
00:32:00.310 --> 00:32:06.130
According to Jamesopedia, they had two days and a little more, like two days and a half

760
00:32:06.130 --> 00:32:07.490
to shoot the driving scenes.

761
00:32:07.870 --> 00:32:13.070
They shot mostly on the 118 freeway, a little bit on Burbank Boulevard.

762
00:32:13.290 --> 00:32:15.710
That's how we made it look like the East CoaSt.

