00:42:51.510 --> 00:42:51.930
Yes.

1026
00:42:52.230 --> 00:42:53.370
I looked it up.

1027
00:42:53.530 --> 00:42:53.790
Mm-hmm.

1028
00:42:54.250 --> 00:43:01.250
According to the Cornell Acapella Advisory Council, there is a Cornell Acapella Advisory Council.

1029
00:43:01.830 --> 00:43:02.250
Amazing.

1030
00:43:02.250 --> 00:43:08.390
There are not any current acapella groups with those names, but I'm not sure about when we filmed.

1031
00:43:08.690 --> 00:43:09.290
Aca what?

1032
00:43:09.650 --> 00:43:10.990
Aca, let me tell you.

1033
00:43:11.390 --> 00:43:16.370
Veda said that Rain was improvising quite a bit in this moment.

1034
00:43:16.630 --> 00:43:16.910
Oh.

1035
00:43:17.070 --> 00:43:19.570
Some was scripted, and then he just started going off.

1036
00:43:19.710 --> 00:43:20.330
I see.

1037
00:43:20.330 --> 00:43:28.950
Yes, and also Anthony shared that he pitched that Stanley should be the first person to come out of the bathroom to kind of throw Andy off.

1038
00:43:29.090 --> 00:43:29.170
Yeah.

1039
00:43:29.170 --> 00:43:31.530
Because Andy's so ready, and then Stanley comes out, and he's like, ugh.

1040
00:43:31.750 --> 00:43:34.090
And then he has to get his energy back up for Dwight.

1041
00:43:34.290 --> 00:43:35.810
I love that little moment.

1042
00:43:35.930 --> 00:43:36.470
Great detail.

1043
00:43:37.010 --> 00:43:49.530
All of this is going to lead to a delicious scene in the conference room, because Andy informs Dwight, guess who is conducting your interview?

1044
00:43:49.530 --> 00:43:50.110
Mm-hmm.

1045
00:43:50.270 --> 00:43:53.190
He's contacted Cornell, and he's going to do the interview.

1046
00:43:53.610 --> 00:43:53.810
Yeah.

1047
00:43:53.990 --> 00:43:55.690
And Dwight's like, bring it on.

1048
00:43:56.050 --> 00:43:58.030
I love this conference room scene so much.

1049
00:43:58.130 --> 00:43:59.630
I love it so much.

1050
00:43:59.850 --> 00:44:05.790
Dave shared that this conference room scene between Dwight and Andy was his first day of filming.

1051
00:44:06.250 --> 00:44:06.650
What?

1052
00:44:06.930 --> 00:44:10.410
Yes, and he loved that because it was so contained, right?

1053
00:44:10.710 --> 00:44:12.310
Oh, my gosh, yes.

1054
00:44:12.530 --> 00:44:12.810
Right?

1055
00:44:13.110 --> 00:44:15.970
And he said it was about a 10 to 11-page scene.

1056
00:44:16.110 --> 00:44:17.490
That's a huge scene.

1057
00:44:17.490 --> 00:44:21.530
Yes, a lot of people asked, was this scripted or improvised?

1058
00:44:21.530 --> 00:44:24.050
It was almost all scripted.

1059
00:44:24.150 --> 00:44:32.530
It was almost all scripted, but Veda said that they did let Rain and Ed really play around, especially with the role model name pitches.

1060
00:44:32.770 --> 00:44:33.110
Mm-hmm.

1061
00:44:33.230 --> 00:44:35.830
And these guys kept laughing.

1062
00:44:36.250 --> 00:44:38.750
They were breaking so hard in this scene.

1063
00:44:38.750 --> 00:44:46.510
In the end, Dwight says his role models are Dane Cook, Jack Bauer, and Eli Whitney, but in the script, they're different.

1064
00:44:46.670 --> 00:44:46.990
Mm-hmm.

1065
00:44:47.170 --> 00:44:50.110
And there's many takes of these names being different.

1066
00:44:50.270 --> 00:44:56.450
But there was one big part of this scene that was improvised, and Anthony talks about it.

1067
00:44:56.570 --> 00:44:57.370
It's so good.

1068
00:44:57.870 --> 00:45:03.610
That scene that we had in the conference room where they were, the double interview, as it were,

1069
00:45:03.810 --> 00:45:09.430
that had always been in there as a fun scene for the two of them to square off at the end of that episode.

1070
00:45:09.950 --> 00:45:19.190
I do remember there was a moment where it was either Rain or Ed started pulling the table, and I was just like, oh, we've got to do that more.

1071
00:45:19.610 --> 00:45:27.950
So I talked to Dave Rogers, who was directing his first episode of The Office, and he's directed a thousand things since because he's freaking amazing.

1072
00:45:28.330 --> 00:45:29.150
I remember talking to him.

1073
00:45:29.230 --> 00:45:34.670
I was like, they've got to just let him play with that table, let him pull it back and forth, let him struggle with that and see what happens.

1074
00:45:34.670 --> 00:45:42.990
And I think we got, that was the only take I think we did of that, where Rain just pulls it all the way to the wall and thanks him for coming.

1075
00:45:43.170 --> 00:45:49.170
It's just that whole, you know, those characters are all about conflict, all about power shifts, and that whole dynamic,

1076
00:45:49.170 --> 00:45:52.890
it felt like the right place to end up with those characters.

1077
00:45:52.890 --> 00:45:57.350
And so that was a nice little bit of improv that we got to enhance on the day.

1078
00:45:58.270 --> 00:46:02.230
I feel like Dave must have been so excited after this first shoot day.

1079
00:46:02.390 --> 00:46:02.670
Yeah.

1080
00:46:02.670 --> 00:46:07.870
To get that table-tugging moment, to get this whole scene, these guys are so good in it.

1081
00:46:08.010 --> 00:46:08.230
Yeah.

1082
00:46:08.510 --> 00:46:09.970
He had to have been fired up.

1083
00:46:10.150 --> 00:46:11.170
You would think so.

1084
00:46:11.350 --> 00:46:15.490
I mean, the biggest stuff was ahead of him, but at least he had that first day in the conference room.

1085
00:46:15.630 --> 00:46:22.090
Well, you know, it's interesting, Dave shared with me, the last thing we shot for this episode was the Halloween cold open.

1086
00:46:22.270 --> 00:46:24.030
That was the last day of shooting.

1087
00:46:24.230 --> 00:46:24.590
Oh, wow.

1088
00:46:24.890 --> 00:46:25.190
Yeah.

1089
00:46:25.190 --> 00:46:29.270
He said we needed time to get all those costumes and everything organized.

1090
00:46:29.630 --> 00:46:29.830
Yeah.

1091
00:46:30.270 --> 00:46:32.450
Should we talk about what's going on with Jim and Pam?

1092
00:46:32.670 --> 00:46:33.850
During all of this now?

1093
00:46:34.070 --> 00:46:34.470
Yes.

1094
00:46:34.710 --> 00:46:37.510
So we know that they're going to have lunch with Jim's brothers.

1095
00:46:37.770 --> 00:46:40.850
But what we find out is that Pam gets to the restaurant early.

1096
00:46:41.490 --> 00:46:43.030
She wants to do a prank.

1097
00:46:43.290 --> 00:46:44.890
Because she wants them to like her.

1098
00:46:45.130 --> 00:46:45.350
Yeah.

1099
00:46:45.490 --> 00:46:47.550
She's like going to be the fun sister-in-law.

1100
00:46:48.050 --> 00:46:49.350
Jenna, do you have a guest star breakdown?

1101
00:46:49.690 --> 00:46:50.610
You know I do.

1102
00:46:50.610 --> 00:46:58.550
Pete Halpert was played by Tug Coker, and Tom Halpert was played by Blake Robbins.

1103
00:46:58.730 --> 00:46:59.970
They were super tall.

1104
00:47:00.230 --> 00:47:01.290
Very tall.

1105
00:47:01.670 --> 00:47:03.250
There's the reason for that.

1106
00:47:03.690 --> 00:47:11.490
John Krasinski has two very tall brothers in real life, and they thought this would be a fun nod to his family.

1107
00:47:11.730 --> 00:47:12.030
Yeah.

1108
00:47:12.890 --> 00:47:15.690
I was able to get in touch with Tug, by the way.

1109
00:47:16.090 --> 00:47:19.290
And oh my gosh, I could not love this guy more.

1110
00:47:19.390 --> 00:47:23.230
I mean, we had such a fun time shooting together, and I had so much fun reminiscing with him about this.

1111
00:47:23.450 --> 00:47:32.990
He told me that the audition notice for this episode, it said it was looking for actors who were six foot one or taller, preferably with brown hair.

1112
00:47:32.990 --> 00:47:36.310
But it did not reveal that you would be playing Jim Halpert's brother.

1113
00:47:37.370 --> 00:47:42.230
And when he got to the audition, he said, first of all, he's six foot five.

1114
00:47:42.490 --> 00:47:48.190
And when he got to the audition, Allison Jones said, you look like you could play John Krasinski's brother.

1115
00:47:48.690 --> 00:47:49.590
That's what she said.

1116
00:47:49.670 --> 00:47:52.350
And he was like, oh, I'm going to be playing a helper.

1117
00:47:52.730 --> 00:47:52.990
Yeah.

1118
00:47:52.990 --> 00:47:54.370
That was his first clue.

1119
00:47:54.710 --> 00:47:57.390
He read with Allison's associate, Ben Harris.

1120
00:47:57.930 --> 00:48:01.150
And the next day, he got a call that he'd gotten the part.

1121
00:48:01.150 --> 00:48:05.030
Well, I definitely felt like these guys look like they could be John's brothers.

1122
00:48:05.310 --> 00:48:08.090
And you know, John's brothers in real life are super tall.

1123
00:48:08.310 --> 00:48:09.430
They're like 6'8 or something.

1124
00:48:09.670 --> 00:48:10.850
They're like the tallest family.

1125
00:48:11.150 --> 00:48:12.510
Isn't John the short one?

1126
00:48:12.610 --> 00:48:13.010
Yes.

1127
00:48:13.390 --> 00:48:14.610
And John is 6'3.

1128
00:48:14.790 --> 00:48:15.990
Yeah, and he's the shorty.

1129
00:48:17.350 --> 00:48:18.470
That is so crazy.

1130
00:48:18.870 --> 00:48:23.170
Well, Tug said, here's the thing that happens when you're a really tall actor.

1131
00:48:23.690 --> 00:48:25.670
You usually have to bring your own clothes.

1132
00:48:25.970 --> 00:48:28.890
Listen, Tug, that's what happens when you're a really short actor, too.

1133
00:48:29.070 --> 00:48:30.110
Angela can relate.

1134
00:48:30.110 --> 00:48:33.910
He said that is his own suit, and those are his own shoes.

1135
00:48:34.170 --> 00:48:34.970
I believe it.

1136
00:48:35.070 --> 00:48:38.510
He's pretty sure that Blake wore his own clothes in the scene as well.

1137
00:48:38.810 --> 00:48:42.450
So you know this first scene at the restaurant, Angela, where Pam has met them early,

1138
00:48:42.610 --> 00:48:46.050
and she's pitching her idea for what the prank could be.

1139
00:48:46.350 --> 00:48:49.350
She says her ring, she put it in her little apron.

1140
00:48:49.710 --> 00:48:50.930
She left it.

1141
00:48:51.210 --> 00:48:53.250
She's going to throw another girl under the bus.

1142
00:48:53.470 --> 00:48:55.850
This whole drama, she lost her engagement ring.

1143
00:48:56.150 --> 00:48:58.550
And they're like, oh, we have a better idea.

1144
00:48:59.090 --> 00:49:04.990
Their idea is that they're going to dog Pam about her career choice as an artiSt.

1145
00:49:05.330 --> 00:49:09.230
Yeah, and they said, let's do the same thing we did to Jim's girlfriend in high school.

1146
00:49:09.510 --> 00:49:10.930
What the heck, guys?

1147
00:49:11.110 --> 00:49:12.770
What is your pattern here?

1148
00:49:12.970 --> 00:49:17.770
Oh, our bit is we make the girls that Jim's dating feel crappy about themselves.

1149
00:49:17.990 --> 00:49:18.690
I know!

1150
00:49:19.010 --> 00:49:19.990
What the heck?

1151
00:49:19.990 --> 00:49:20.550
I know!

1152
00:49:20.730 --> 00:49:25.590
They said in the DVD commentary that they wanted Jim's brothers to be bad at pranking.

1153
00:49:25.730 --> 00:49:28.990
Like, they're like the less sophisticated prankers of the family.

1154
00:49:29.250 --> 00:49:30.790
Jim is better at pranking.

1155
00:49:30.930 --> 00:49:32.250
They're kind of lame at it.

1156
00:49:32.450 --> 00:49:35.110
So most of this stuff was scripted in the restaurant.

1157
00:49:35.110 --> 00:49:38.130
We did not have a lot of time, actually, to play around.

1158
00:49:38.510 --> 00:49:43.350
But Tug reminded me that we did improvise the very end of this scene.

1159
00:49:43.350 --> 00:49:48.790
And he said, Jenna, I'm pretty sure you improvised that line, so not the ring thing then.

1160
00:49:49.350 --> 00:49:52.770
And then the two of them are like, no, no, no, this is better.

1161
00:49:52.850 --> 00:49:53.290
This is better.

1162
00:49:53.430 --> 00:49:55.090
And I checked the script, and he's right.

1163
00:49:55.210 --> 00:49:57.670
The scene had actually been meant to end sooner.

1164
00:49:57.950 --> 00:50:00.290
That sounds like you in real life, by the way.

1165
00:50:00.410 --> 00:50:02.050
That sounds like something you would say.

1166
00:50:02.170 --> 00:50:02.950
Maybe so.

1167
00:50:03.110 --> 00:50:06.650
I feel like we've ordered lunch together, and I've gone back and forth about an appetizer.

1168
00:50:06.770 --> 00:50:09.390
And you've said, so not the dip then.

1169
00:50:09.550 --> 00:50:10.730
We're not doing the dip.

1170
00:50:10.810 --> 00:50:11.290
Just to clarify.

1171
00:50:12.390 --> 00:50:18.490
Well, Dave shared that you guys filmed this restaurant scene the day after Labor Day.

1172
00:50:18.750 --> 00:50:19.150
Oh.

1173
00:50:19.470 --> 00:50:20.850
Tuesday in September.

1174
00:50:20.850 --> 00:50:23.030
I thought that was a fun little detail to know.

1175
00:50:23.250 --> 00:50:27.510
And Kyle, the locations manager, said that this restaurant was called E3rd.

1176
00:50:27.710 --> 00:50:28.070
Mm-hmm.

1177
00:50:28.190 --> 00:50:30.710
And it was on the east side of downtown LA.

1178
00:50:31.010 --> 00:50:35.450
They were really trying to get this area to double as Brooklyn, where Pam was attending Pratt.

1179
00:50:35.670 --> 00:50:36.910
I think they did a good job.

1180
00:50:37.050 --> 00:50:37.210
Yeah.

1181
00:50:37.510 --> 00:50:39.690
Well, the restaurant was a steakhouse.

1182
00:50:39.910 --> 00:50:40.430
Mm-hmm.

1183
00:50:40.990 --> 00:50:46.710
And in the next scene, where you see that we're eating, after Jim has arrived, we got

1184
00:50:46.710 --> 00:50:47.810
to just pick off the menu.

1185
00:50:47.810 --> 00:50:50.110
Oh, so you're really eating the restaurant food?

1186
00:50:50.250 --> 00:50:50.430
Yeah.

1187
00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:51.670
Oh, that's so lucky.

1188
00:50:51.870 --> 00:50:52.350
I know.

1189
00:50:52.530 --> 00:50:53.290
Oh, that's cool.

1190
00:50:53.550 --> 00:50:58.790
Well, Tug said he remembers it very clearly because it was the very first time he had to

1191
00:50:58.790 --> 00:50:59.770
eat in a scene.

1192
00:50:59.950 --> 00:51:04.910
And when they gave him the menu, he thought his character would order steak at a steakhouse.

1193
00:51:05.150 --> 00:51:09.310
And that John Krasinski said, oh, dude, you're going to regret that choice.

1194
00:51:09.570 --> 00:51:12.530
You're going to be eating cold steak for several hours.

1195
00:51:12.990 --> 00:51:14.450
And Tug was like, what do you mean?

1196
00:51:14.490 --> 00:51:15.430
I'm going to eat steak.

1197
00:51:15.430 --> 00:51:16.810
And that's what my character would eat.

1198
00:51:16.910 --> 00:51:18.590
And he said, John ordered a salad.

1199
00:51:18.790 --> 00:51:19.150
Mm-hmm.

1200
00:51:19.410 --> 00:51:21.270
And like a little protein on the side.

1201
00:51:21.330 --> 00:51:22.810
And that's what I ordered as well.

1202
00:51:23.390 --> 00:51:28.870
Well, Tug said that his concern about ordering a salad was that he didn't want any food to

1203
00:51:28.870 --> 00:51:30.870
fall on him during the scene.

1204
00:51:30.990 --> 00:51:32.890
He was like, this is the first time I'm eating and acting.

1205
00:51:32.890 --> 00:51:35.310
I think steak, I can get it on the fork.

1206
00:51:35.470 --> 00:51:36.490
I can get it in my mouth.

1207
00:51:36.670 --> 00:51:39.070
Well, steak is definitely easier to eat than salad.

1208
00:51:39.630 --> 00:51:44.190
Well, Tug pointed out to me, and I didn't notice it the first time I watched it.

1209
00:51:44.250 --> 00:51:48.930
But he said it's burned in his brain because this is the scene that was on his acting reel

1210
00:51:48.930 --> 00:51:49.870
for years and years.

1211
00:51:50.510 --> 00:51:56.510
So at 12 minutes, 25 seconds, John is struggling with this bite of salad.

1212
00:51:56.510 --> 00:51:57.470
You can see it.

1213
00:51:57.610 --> 00:51:58.430
I saw that too.

1214
00:51:58.430 --> 00:52:01.450
He's having a very hard time getting this piece of lettuce in his mouth.

1215
00:52:01.770 --> 00:52:09.070
And then, if you watch closely, one leaf misses his mouth and falls into his lap, which

1216
00:52:09.070 --> 00:52:14.050
was exactly Tug's fear, that if Tug had been eating salad, he would have missed his

1217
00:52:14.050 --> 00:52:14.410
mouth.

1218
00:52:15.010 --> 00:52:18.490
He was then glad he had ordered that steak and had to eat it for hours.

1219
00:52:18.810 --> 00:52:23.010
John, as I rewatched that, I thought, that's a really big, aggressive bite of lettuce.

1220
00:52:23.230 --> 00:52:24.530
Like, he really went for it.

1221
00:52:24.650 --> 00:52:25.110
He did.

1222
00:52:25.270 --> 00:52:28.250
You know, sometimes when you're eating salad in a scene, you don't realize what

1223
00:52:28.250 --> 00:52:30.750
you've got on the fork, and then you just have to commit to it.

1224
00:52:31.730 --> 00:52:33.330
And that was on Tug's reel.

1225
00:52:33.550 --> 00:52:35.210
So he watched it over and over.

1226
00:52:35.330 --> 00:52:37.470
Over and over again, he watched that piece of lettuce fall.

1227
00:52:38.150 --> 00:52:41.070
So you know their dinner starts out pretty sweet, right?

1228
00:52:41.230 --> 00:52:44.310
Jim is holding up a photo of his niece, right?

1229
00:52:44.570 --> 00:52:44.750
Yeah.

1230
00:52:45.030 --> 00:52:47.010
So you feel like this is going to be nice.

1231
00:52:47.010 --> 00:52:47.950
It's pre-prank.

1232
00:52:48.050 --> 00:52:49.270
The prank hasn't started yet.

1233
00:52:49.270 --> 00:52:50.370
The prank hasn't started yet.

1234
00:52:50.670 --> 00:52:55.870
The photo that John is holding up is our set medic, Patrice King's daughter.

1235
00:52:55.870 --> 00:52:58.130
Oh, yeah, Phil shared that.

1236
00:52:58.290 --> 00:52:59.570
Phil would do that, you guys.

1237
00:53:00.030 --> 00:53:04.890
This scene also has the moment where all of us, at the end of the scene, give a look to

1238
00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:05.250
camera.

1239
00:53:05.730 --> 00:53:07.630
And it's such a cool moment.

1240
00:53:08.230 --> 00:53:12.970
Tug said he remembers Dave Roger giving him the direction to check in with the camera throughout

1241
00:53:12.970 --> 00:53:13.510
the scene.

1242
00:53:13.610 --> 00:53:17.590
And this was, like, so crazy to him because, you know, he'd never been in a project where

1243
00:53:17.590 --> 00:53:19.570
you were allowed to look down the lens like that.

1244
00:53:19.570 --> 00:53:21.230
But I love this moment.

1245
00:53:21.450 --> 00:53:25.710
I love the look that he gives the camera and you just go around the table and we all give

1246
00:53:25.710 --> 00:53:29.970
this little look to camera about this prank that is not going well.

1247
00:53:30.270 --> 00:53:30.870
Not going well.

1248
00:53:31.130 --> 00:53:32.870
Dave talked about it a little bit.

1249
00:53:33.010 --> 00:53:37.510
He said he wanted the brothers to look to camera to just give that subtle hint that their

1250
00:53:37.510 --> 00:53:41.590
mannerisms were similar to Jim, that they would check in like that.

1251
00:53:41.790 --> 00:53:45.170
At 8 minutes, 33 seconds, Pete gives a solo look to camera.

1252
00:53:45.170 --> 00:53:51.010
And at 12 minutes, 31 seconds, Tom gives a Jim kind of shrug to camera.

1253
00:53:51.190 --> 00:53:52.130
I loved that one.

1254
00:53:52.330 --> 00:53:53.630
I thought that was so good.

1255
00:53:53.870 --> 00:53:58.110
Well, as this prank continues, it is really getting under Pam's skin.

1256
00:53:58.330 --> 00:54:00.490
Like, she is getting very flustered.

1257
00:54:00.490 --> 00:54:07.150
I think particularly when he suggests that she pay the bill by drawing on the napkin.

1258
00:54:07.550 --> 00:54:15.110
Oh, Jenna, if you need a boost, listen to the DVD commentary because Veda said she was

1259
00:54:15.110 --> 00:54:16.710
so impressed with your performance.

1260
00:54:17.070 --> 00:54:17.470
Aw.

1261
00:54:17.730 --> 00:54:22.550
She said, you know, the way this was scripted is tough because Pam has to want to be on

1262
00:54:22.550 --> 00:54:27.250
board to be pranked, but then also start clocking like, hey, that's kind of a dig.

1263
00:54:27.410 --> 00:54:28.650
Okay, you're kind of going too far.

1264
00:54:28.850 --> 00:54:31.710
And she said, Jenna did such an amazing job.

1265
00:54:31.990 --> 00:54:32.890
It was really sweet.

1266
00:54:33.130 --> 00:54:34.290
Veda was showing you some love.

1267
00:54:34.530 --> 00:54:35.430
That's really sweet.

1268
00:54:35.630 --> 00:54:40.610
Well, it was kind of a fine line because everything that Veda said, part of the storyline

1269
00:54:40.610 --> 00:54:47.350
was also meant to further Pam's insecurity about the idea of being an artiSt.

1270
00:54:48.310 --> 00:54:54.010
And, you know, because this is something that she wants, but Pam is not a person with a

1271
00:54:54.010 --> 00:54:56.350
lot of certainty all the time.

1272
00:54:56.350 --> 00:54:58.390
And this was supposed to play on that.

1273
00:54:58.770 --> 00:55:02.030
It was a lot for Pam to go to art school.

1274
00:55:02.130 --> 00:55:02.870
It really was.

1275
00:55:03.010 --> 00:55:03.290
Yeah.

1276
00:55:03.290 --> 00:55:06.890
And so this is meant to kind of discourage her momentum.

1277
00:55:07.530 --> 00:55:08.890
Aw, that makes me sad.

1278
00:55:08.990 --> 00:55:09.350
Yeah.

1279
00:55:09.610 --> 00:55:10.230
I know.

1280
00:55:10.330 --> 00:55:10.710
I know.

1281
00:55:11.050 --> 00:55:16.370
I have to say, it was so nice reconnecting with Tug about these scenes.

1282
00:55:16.670 --> 00:55:18.730
You know, he said he's still in touch with Blake.

1283
00:55:18.770 --> 00:55:22.250
He still gets recognized for having been on the show.

1284
00:55:22.430 --> 00:55:22.670
Aw.

1285
00:55:22.950 --> 00:55:29.610
Something he told me that I thought was really special was that the day this episode aired,

1286
00:55:30.510 --> 00:55:37.890
Dave Rogers called him personally, complimented his performance, and told him, hey, I wanted

1287
00:55:37.890 --> 00:55:41.730
you to know that the bulk of the brothers' scenes made it into the episode.

1288
00:55:42.050 --> 00:55:44.670
And so when you see it tonight, it's there.

1289
00:55:44.890 --> 00:55:46.010
That is so nice.

1290
00:55:46.170 --> 00:55:47.110
No one does that.

1291
00:55:47.250 --> 00:55:48.550
That was so nice of Dave.

1292
00:55:48.810 --> 00:55:50.010
No one does that.

1293
00:55:50.210 --> 00:55:53.690
And Tug said, you know, I'd done a ton of guest roles.

1294
00:55:53.830 --> 00:55:57.710
And sometimes you tell your whole family to watch it, and they watch it, and your whole

1295
00:55:57.710 --> 00:55:59.350
part has been reduced to one line.

1296
00:55:59.350 --> 00:56:00.150
All the time.

1297
00:56:00.270 --> 00:56:02.550
He said, so he was so excited.

1298
00:56:02.890 --> 00:56:06.570
He called his friends and family, and he was like, yes, yes, watch the show.

1299
00:56:06.570 --> 00:56:07.730
I'm really on it.

1300
00:56:07.990 --> 00:56:09.870
And the show was a big deal at the time.

1301
00:56:10.030 --> 00:56:13.570
This was a big deal to him and his friends and family that he had been on it.

1302
00:56:13.850 --> 00:56:16.750
So Dave Rogers, you are a gem.

1303
00:56:17.450 --> 00:56:18.870
Tug, thank you so much.

1304
00:56:19.050 --> 00:56:22.850
I want you guys to know that you can catch him on a show called Now We're Talking.

1305
00:56:22.850 --> 00:56:29.950
It is a scripted comedy series, and he co-created it, produced it, and stars in it.

1306
00:56:30.050 --> 00:56:33.110
And it was nominated for a WGA award.

1307
00:56:33.350 --> 00:56:38.450
It's produced by LeBron James and Maverick Carter's company Spring Hill.

1308
00:56:38.450 --> 00:56:43.250
But Office fans, if you check it out, you might see some Office alums on there.

1309
00:56:43.430 --> 00:56:46.530
They've got Malcolm Barrett and Andy Buckley pop up on the show.

1310
00:56:46.950 --> 00:56:47.070
Nice.

1311
00:56:47.370 --> 00:56:49.910
So definitely check it out, because this guy is amazing.

1312
00:56:50.070 --> 00:56:51.470
Tug, thank you so much.

1313
00:56:51.970 --> 00:56:53.810
So we finish out this Jim and Pam storyline.

1314
00:56:54.070 --> 00:56:56.190
They're leaving the restaurant, and the two of them are walking down the street.

1315
00:56:56.310 --> 00:56:58.450
And Pam's like, that's not exactly how I had that going.

1316
00:56:58.710 --> 00:56:58.830
Yeah.

1317
00:56:58.910 --> 00:57:01.430
Like, I had a whole different prank, and she tells it to him.

1318
00:57:01.690 --> 00:57:05.930
And then Jenna, Veda shared that you ad-libbed the end.

1319
00:57:06.310 --> 00:57:08.070
The line about him being bald.

1320
00:57:08.430 --> 00:57:09.250
You ad-libbed.

1321
00:57:09.270 --> 00:57:11.950
How about we prank him on Thanksgiving about him being bald?

1322
00:57:12.250 --> 00:57:13.290
That was all you.

1323
00:57:14.370 --> 00:57:15.870
I was really proud of that line.

1324
00:57:15.870 --> 00:57:16.750
I thought that was funny.

1325
00:57:16.890 --> 00:57:17.910
Yeah, it was really funny.

1326
00:57:17.910 --> 00:57:19.710
So you had some improvs in this one, lady.

1327
00:57:19.710 --> 00:57:20.390
I did.

1328
00:57:20.650 --> 00:57:21.370
I really did.

1329
00:57:21.990 --> 00:57:26.150
Now I think we should wrap up this Michael and Holly storyline,

1330
00:57:26.690 --> 00:57:31.550
because they've arrived at Holly's charming little house in Nashua.

1331
00:57:31.890 --> 00:57:32.350
I know.

1332
00:57:32.490 --> 00:57:35.790
Anthony said in the script he wanted it to be a basement apartment.

1333
00:57:36.010 --> 00:57:36.390
Oh.

1334
00:57:36.570 --> 00:57:39.470
But he was like, but we don't really have basement apartments here.

1335
00:57:39.890 --> 00:57:43.470
So they found this little house in Angeleno Heights.

1336
00:57:43.870 --> 00:57:44.310
Oh.

1337
00:57:44.570 --> 00:57:45.530
Isn't it so cute?

1338
00:57:45.530 --> 00:57:46.570
I thought it was so cute.

1339
00:57:46.770 --> 00:57:49.290
It brought up a lot of questions for me, though.

1340
00:57:50.010 --> 00:57:55.610
If Holly was in Nashua and she had to move her whole life and all her stuff

1341
00:57:55.610 --> 00:57:59.650
and get rid of her house slash apartment that she had been living in

1342
00:57:59.650 --> 00:58:05.670
and move to Scranton, she was only in Scranton for, I think, like less than two months.

1343
00:58:06.010 --> 00:58:08.290
And now she has to move all the way back.

1344
00:58:08.310 --> 00:58:10.070
And it was kind of breaking my heart for her.

1345
00:58:10.070 --> 00:58:17.890
I was glad they picked a cute location because I was thinking, oh my gosh, she just left this city.

1346
00:58:18.450 --> 00:58:24.030
But then I thought it tracks that she would know where to get a cute place if she was from there.

1347
00:58:24.830 --> 00:58:26.770
Maybe it's even her old place.

1348
00:58:27.150 --> 00:58:28.050
Maybe it is.

1349
00:58:28.110 --> 00:58:29.030
It's super cute.

1350
00:58:29.290 --> 00:58:29.770
Super cute.

1351
00:58:29.770 --> 00:58:33.570
Also, per Dave, they were really stressed about losing light.

1352
00:58:33.910 --> 00:58:39.590
And they were going to be losing some of the crew because they were going to leave to go film

1353
00:58:39.590 --> 00:58:43.310
the Jim and Pam proposal scene with Ken Kwapis.

1354
00:58:43.710 --> 00:58:43.950
Yeah.

1355
00:58:44.310 --> 00:58:46.490
So we would do this sometimes.

1356
00:58:47.210 --> 00:58:52.690
We filmed the Jim-Pam proposal during this episode's week of filming.

1357
00:58:52.950 --> 00:58:53.190
Right.

1358
00:58:53.270 --> 00:58:54.410
Because they had to build the whole thing.

1359
00:58:54.510 --> 00:58:56.910
Sometimes the schedule just got wonky like that.

1360
00:58:56.910 --> 00:59:00.750
But so Dave was really on a time crunch here to get this filmed.

1361
00:59:01.390 --> 00:59:03.930
Well, Michael decides he's not going to stay.

1362
00:59:04.150 --> 00:59:06.110
He had planned to stay for the weekend.

1363
00:59:06.450 --> 00:59:11.710
I guess to help her unpack, it seems pretty clear that they're going to break up.

1364
00:59:11.870 --> 00:59:12.330
Yeah.

1365
00:59:12.890 --> 00:59:16.930
Because of the seven-hour drive that's really a five-hour drive.

1366
00:59:16.930 --> 00:59:17.790
Only four hours.

1367
00:59:18.210 --> 00:59:18.770
Four and a half.

1368
00:59:18.890 --> 00:59:19.750
They could have totally done it.

1369
00:59:19.770 --> 00:59:20.530
They could have done it.

1370
00:59:20.710 --> 00:59:23.770
I wanted to go into the TV and tell them.

1371
00:59:23.770 --> 00:59:29.630
But Anthony said that he wrote dialogue here for them saying goodbye and how, well, maybe

1372
00:59:29.630 --> 00:59:31.470
I'll see you or maybe we'll go in this and that.

1373
00:59:31.610 --> 00:59:37.230
And then in the moment, Amy and Steve just did this really big, long, lingering hug.

1374
00:59:37.590 --> 00:59:39.490
And Dave was like, that's it.

1375
00:59:40.110 --> 00:59:40.270
Yeah.

1376
00:59:40.630 --> 00:59:42.070
They don't need to have the dialogue.

1377
00:59:42.290 --> 00:59:43.870
That hug tells you everything.

1378
00:59:43.870 --> 00:59:46.630
We had a lot of mail.

1379
00:59:46.970 --> 00:59:47.610
Oh, yeah?

1380
00:59:48.070 --> 00:59:55.870
From Chris W., Chelsea C., Hanlon H., and many others just asking a couple of questions.

1381
00:59:56.570 --> 01:00:03.750
Number one, how was Michael planning to get back to Scranton if he and Holly hadn't broken up?

1382
01:00:03.970 --> 01:00:04.390
Right.

1383
01:00:04.650 --> 01:00:05.890
Neither of them have a car.

1384
01:00:06.150 --> 01:00:07.550
That was the other thing.

1385
01:00:07.790 --> 01:00:10.610
Did Holly not bring a car to Nashua?

1386
01:00:10.930 --> 01:00:12.470
What'd she do with her car?

1387
01:00:12.470 --> 01:00:14.310
Did she leave it in Scranton?

1388
01:00:14.530 --> 01:00:15.290
I don't know.

1389
01:00:15.290 --> 01:00:16.290
They didn't tow it.

1390
01:00:16.490 --> 01:00:16.850
No.

1391
01:00:16.970 --> 01:00:17.290
I noticed.

1392
01:00:17.450 --> 01:00:18.310
I looked for it.

1393
01:00:18.450 --> 01:00:18.850
Mm-hmm.

1394
01:00:19.270 --> 01:00:26.370
Poor Holly has just gotten dropped off with all her stuff, a mattress in, like, you know,

1395
01:00:26.490 --> 01:00:27.370
plastic wrap.

1396
01:00:27.990 --> 01:00:31.150
No one is helping her unpack, and she has no car.

1397
01:00:31.290 --> 01:00:33.070
And she's dressed for work.

1398
01:00:33.330 --> 01:00:33.670
Yeah.

1399
01:00:33.970 --> 01:00:35.750
That's how we leave Holly in Nashua.

1400
01:00:35.990 --> 01:00:36.610
I know.

1401
01:00:36.610 --> 01:00:45.390
Oh, this whole storyline ends with such an amazing scene of Michael and Daryl in the car driving back.

1402
01:00:46.030 --> 01:00:49.150
Dave was really stressed because, like you said, they were losing light.

1403
01:00:49.510 --> 01:00:49.670
Yeah.

1404
01:00:49.770 --> 01:00:53.370
He said Randall, our camera operator, was going, come on, we got to get this now.

1405
01:00:53.470 --> 01:00:54.290
We got to get it now.

1406
01:00:54.570 --> 01:00:57.990
The sun was setting, but didn't it make for such a beautiful backdrop?

1407
01:00:58.330 --> 01:00:58.610
Yes.

1408
01:00:58.850 --> 01:01:01.010
It just meant that they didn't get a lot of takes.

1409
01:01:01.010 --> 01:01:02.270
They had to nail it.

1410
01:01:02.650 --> 01:01:06.710
Anthony said he loved that it was getting dark because you really got the sense that

1411
01:01:06.710 --> 01:01:08.850
they spent the whole day together.

1412
01:01:09.250 --> 01:01:10.350
I liked that, too.

1413
01:01:10.850 --> 01:01:13.630
Dave told me this is his favorite scene from the episode.

1414
01:01:14.230 --> 01:01:15.310
Anthony said the same thing.

1415
01:01:15.610 --> 01:01:15.750
Yeah.

1416
01:01:15.930 --> 01:01:19.110
Anthony was very excited because this was his pitch and his idea.

1417
01:01:19.330 --> 01:01:20.590
He talks about it right here.

1418
01:01:21.250 --> 01:01:21.510
Yeah.

1419
01:01:21.650 --> 01:01:26.530
This is my first ever episode of television that was written and got onto TV, so it holds

1420
01:01:26.530 --> 01:01:29.070
a very near and dear place in my heart, this one.

1421
01:01:29.070 --> 01:01:31.330
And all the stuff with the breakup.

1422
01:01:31.510 --> 01:01:36.190
And oh, the thing with, oh my God, of course, the scene at the end where Michael's singing

1423
01:01:36.190 --> 01:01:39.350
the blues, that's a special moment for me in particular because I do remember pitching

1424
01:01:39.350 --> 01:01:40.030
that in the room.

1425
01:01:40.230 --> 01:01:44.130
And it's one of those things as a writer, so many things you pitch, they might end up

1426
01:01:44.130 --> 01:01:46.130
in other people's scripts, but they might end up in your script.

1427
01:01:46.270 --> 01:01:48.510
And you're just trying to tell the story the best way you can.

1428
01:01:48.610 --> 01:01:51.790
And every once in a while, you get a situation where something you pitch is in your script and

1429
01:01:51.790 --> 01:01:54.770
it ends up being on the show and you feel like, oh, that's amazing.

1430
01:01:54.850 --> 01:01:58.690
That whole blues moment at the end when Michael Scott just doesn't get it, but still

1431
01:01:58.690 --> 01:02:00.590
has the cathartic moment he needs at the end of that.

1432
01:02:00.710 --> 01:02:04.510
I thought, I remember pitching that in the room and thinking, oh, that'll be fun to get

1433
01:02:04.510 --> 01:02:04.770
to do.

1434
01:02:04.870 --> 01:02:08.090
And then I got to write the episode and then I got to watch it happen and it was getting

1435
01:02:08.090 --> 01:02:10.750
dark and it was just the perfect little moment for us.

1436
01:02:10.830 --> 01:02:13.830
And I just remember feeling like I have the best job in the world.

1437
01:02:14.950 --> 01:02:16.070
I know those scenes.

1438
01:02:16.650 --> 01:02:17.690
Well, I just love that.

1439
01:02:17.810 --> 01:02:21.410
There was something so special about seeing your idea fully realized.

1440
01:02:22.030 --> 01:02:24.370
And I just love that he shared that.

1441
01:02:24.930 --> 01:02:27.010
Well, lady, we have one last scene.

1442
01:02:27.450 --> 01:02:27.950
We do.

1443
01:02:28.250 --> 01:02:36.930
You know, we don't really ever find out exactly how this Cornell interview application thing

1444
01:02:36.930 --> 01:02:37.490
wraps up.

1445
01:02:37.590 --> 01:02:40.670
I assume he doesn't get in, but that was never really the point.

1446
01:02:40.950 --> 01:02:45.170
The point of this storyline was really Angela.

1447
01:02:45.590 --> 01:02:46.850
Angela was the point.

1448
01:02:47.530 --> 01:02:53.410
Dwight was performing for her and he's winding Andy up because he is jealous.

1449
01:02:53.730 --> 01:02:54.350
That's right.

1450
01:02:54.690 --> 01:02:55.990
Well, there was a whole runner.

1451
01:02:56.330 --> 01:03:01.310
There were scenes between Angela and Andy where Andy's all worked up and Angela's trying to

1452
01:03:01.310 --> 01:03:01.930
calm him down.

1453
01:03:02.110 --> 01:03:04.710
And then Angela goes to Dwight and is like, what the heck?

1454
01:03:05.010 --> 01:03:06.810
Here's one of those deleted scenes.

1455
01:03:09.090 --> 01:03:10.570
Why are you doing this to Andy?

1456
01:03:11.770 --> 01:03:14.490
You once told me that Andy and I had different strengths.

1457
01:03:14.810 --> 01:03:17.310
Well, he can't do what I can do.

1458
01:03:17.910 --> 01:03:21.610
I can get into Cornell, but he doesn't know how to make food and shelter from a golden

1459
01:03:21.610 --> 01:03:22.170
retriever.

1460
01:03:25.240 --> 01:03:28.700
Even if you do somehow get in, that's not going to make me leave Andy.

1461
01:03:30.360 --> 01:03:32.600
No, but it'll make you respect him less.

1462
01:03:35.510 --> 01:03:36.690
Yes, that's true.

1463
01:03:40.790 --> 01:03:41.730
I said it stayed in.

1464
01:03:41.870 --> 01:03:44.910
I know because Dwight does get what he wants, right?

1465
01:03:45.130 --> 01:03:45.310
Yeah.

1466
01:03:45.490 --> 01:03:50.450
I think Andy unravels in front of Angela and whether Dwight gets into Cornell or not,

1467
01:03:50.830 --> 01:03:51.910
she didn't care for it.

1468
01:03:52.150 --> 01:03:53.430
No, not at all.

1469
01:03:53.430 --> 01:03:57.670
And now we have this tag where Andy's going to pay back Dwight.

1470
01:03:57.830 --> 01:03:59.850
But of course, it's just so embarrassing.

1471
01:04:00.110 --> 01:04:03.750
In fact, at 20 minutes, 51 seconds is one of my most popular memes.

1472
01:04:04.190 --> 01:04:04.550
What?

1473
01:04:04.690 --> 01:04:05.830
When you're rolling your eyes?

1474
01:04:06.030 --> 01:04:06.210
Yes.

1475
01:04:06.470 --> 01:04:09.650
Andy walks in dressed as a farmer with no shirt on and beats.

1476
01:04:09.830 --> 01:04:12.990
And my character rolls her eyes and then puts her head into her hand.

1477
01:04:13.330 --> 01:04:15.490
Oh, we had a fan question.

1478
01:04:15.770 --> 01:04:21.170
People wanted to know, did Rain actually take a bite out of a beat at the end of the episode?

1479
01:04:21.590 --> 01:04:22.530
Yes, he did.

1480
01:04:22.630 --> 01:04:23.710
And that was improvised.

1481
01:04:24.190 --> 01:04:24.390
Yes.

1482
01:04:24.550 --> 01:04:26.810
And Veda said he did it in the last take.

1483
01:04:27.170 --> 01:04:29.670
Very smart, Rain, if you're going to do it.

1484
01:04:30.190 --> 01:04:30.610
Yeah.

1485
01:04:30.830 --> 01:04:33.830
It was scripted that Andy tries to bite the beat.

1486
01:04:33.830 --> 01:04:37.150
And that line about, oh, you're supposed to cook it first, that was in the script.

1487
01:04:37.210 --> 01:04:42.530
But the button of Dwight being able to bite a beat, that was all Rain.

1488
01:04:42.750 --> 01:04:43.570
All Rain, Wilson.

1489
01:04:44.650 --> 01:04:47.230
You guys, that was employee transfer.

1490
01:04:47.890 --> 01:04:48.450
Yes.

1491
01:04:48.770 --> 01:04:54.330
And we want to give a huge thanks to all the people who helped gather information on this

1492
01:04:54.330 --> 01:04:54.630
episode.

1493
01:04:54.630 --> 01:04:56.190
It was a bunch of people.

1494
01:04:56.310 --> 01:04:56.810
Thank you.

1495
01:04:57.010 --> 01:05:03.110
Thank you to James Carey, Dave Rogers, Alicia Raycraft, Phil Shea, Anthony Farrell, and

1496
01:05:03.110 --> 01:05:04.990
Tug Corker for sharing your memories.

1497
01:05:05.310 --> 01:05:07.150
One final shout out for Tug.

1498
01:05:07.290 --> 01:05:09.210
He and his wife own a wine bar.

1499
01:05:09.410 --> 01:05:09.790
What?

1500
01:05:09.790 --> 01:05:11.010
Santa Monica, Angela.

1501
01:05:11.330 --> 01:05:12.730
It's called Esther's.

